{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Linear Systems Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gaussian_elimination(A, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Ab = np.hstack([A.astype(float), b.reshape(-1, 1).astype(float)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for k in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_row = k + np.argmax(np.abs(Ab[k:, k]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        Ab[[k, max_row]] = Ab[[max_row, k]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if abs(Ab[k, k]) < 1e-12:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            raise ValueError(f\"Matrix is singular or nearly singular at pivot {k}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(k + 1, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            m = Ab[i, k] / Ab[k, k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            Ab[i, k:] -= m * Ab[k, k:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x[i] = (Ab[i, -1] - Ab[i, i+1:n] @ x[i+1:n]) / Ab[i, i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: LU decomposition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def lu_decompose(A):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = A.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    L = np.eye(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    U = A.astype(float).copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    P = np.eye(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for k in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_row = k + np.argmax(np.abs(U[k:, k]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if max_row != k:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            U[[k, max_row]] = U[[max_row, k]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            P[[k, max_row]] = P[[max_row, k]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if k > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                L[[k, max_row], :k] = L[[max_row, k], :k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(k + 1, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            L[i, k] = U[i, k] / U[k, k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            U[i, k:] -= L[i, k] * U[k, k:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return P, L, U"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def lu_solve(P, L, U, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Pb = P @ b.astype(float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y[i] = Pb[i] - L[i, :i] @ y[:i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x[i] = (y[i] - U[i, i+1:] @ x[i+1:]) / U[i, i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Cholesky decomposition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cholesky(A):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = A.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    L = np.zeros_like(A, dtype=float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(i + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            s = A[i, j] - L[i, :j] @ L[j, :j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if i == j:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if s <= 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    raise ValueError(\"Matrix is not positive definite\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                L[i, j] = np.sqrt(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                L[i, j] = s / L[j, j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return L"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Least squares via normal equations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def least_squares_normal(A, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    AtA = A.T @ A"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Atb = A.T @ b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return gaussian_elimination(AtA, Atb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ridge_regression(A, b, lam):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = A.shape[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    AtA = A.T @ A + lam * np.eye(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Atb = A.T @ b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    L = cholesky(AtA)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y[i] = (Atb[i] - L[i, :i] @ y[:i]) / L[i, i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = np.zeros(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x[i] = (y[i] - L.T[i, i+1:] @ x[i+1:]) / L.T[i, i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Condition number"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def condition_number(A):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    U, S, Vt = np.linalg.svd(A)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return S[0] / S[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Solve the system `[[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,10]] x = [6, 15, 27]` using your Gaussian elimination, your LU solver, and `np.linalg.solve`. Verify all three give the same answer within floating-point tolerance.\n\n2. Generate a 50x5 random matrix X and target y = X @ w_true + noise. Solve for w using normal equations, QR (via `np.linalg.qr`), SVD (via `np.linalg.svd`), and `np.linalg.lstsq`. Compare all four solutions. Measure the condition number of X^T X and explain how it affects which method you trust.\n\n3. Create a nearly singular matrix by making two columns almost identical (e.g., column 2 = column 1 + 1e-10 * noise). Compute its condition number. Solve Ax = b with and without regularization (add 0.01 * I). Compare the solutions and residuals. Explain why regularization helps.\n\n4. Implement the conjugate gradient algorithm for a 100x100 random symmetric positive definite matrix. Count how many iterations it takes to converge to tolerance 1e-8. Compare with the theoretical maximum of n iterations.\n\n5. Time your Cholesky solver vs your LU solver vs `np.linalg.solve` on symmetric positive definite matrices of size 10, 50, 200, 500. Plot the results. Verify Cholesky is roughly 2x faster than LU."
      ]
    }
